    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-17T18:17:44+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-17T18:17:44+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T08:47:44Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-17T08:47:44Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system over the Tasman Sea extends a ridge over South Australia. A trough of low pressure over the northeast of State on Monday gradually moves eastwards and clears to the east later Tuesday. A weakening cold front moves into far southwestern parts later on Tuesday and moves southeast across the state into Wednesday. Another high pressure system develops over the north of the state later Wednesday, with weak troughs clipping the southeast in a broad westerly flow on Thursday and Friday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW011" description="Eastern Eyre Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-17T18:03:31+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T08:33:31Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, becoming less likely at night. The chance of a thunderstorm in the north this evening. Light winds.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the late afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm near the coast in the afternoon and evening. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h increasing to 30 km/h before tending north to northwesterly 20 to 25 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching around 19.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:20am to 2:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 4 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, most likely in the early morning. The chance of a thunderstorm near the coast. Winds northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending westerly 20 to 30 km/h in the middle of the day then becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog. Light winds. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-08-21T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-22T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-20T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-21T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog. Slight chance of a shower. Light winds becoming southerly 15 to 20 km/h during the morning then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching around 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
